WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:05.150
So as we get closer and closer to Election
Day, there are, not surprisingly, some numbers

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:10.910
that are not giving me a high level of confidence
that I know some in my audience already have

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:16.070
about the seemingly inevitable pending victory
of Joseph R. Biden.

00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:17.070
Junior now.

00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:23.039
I already told you last week that as of about
twenty two days out in three key states, Michigan,

00:00:23.039 --> 00:00:28.980
Wisconsin and Pennsylvania, Hillary Clinton
had a bigger lead in 2016 than Joe Biden had

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:30.160
last week.

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:33.010
We will update update those numbers this week.

00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:37.260
But it was a cause for maybe not concern,
but at least for being very, very cautious.

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:42.230
There is another signal that given the realities
of the election, is not a great signal for

00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:43.230
Joe Biden.

00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:47.649
And this is both voter registrations in some
states and mail in ballot requests and even

00:00:47.649 --> 00:00:49.989
early voting numbers in some states.

00:00:49.989 --> 00:00:50.989
And remember why?

00:00:50.989 --> 00:00:53.809
Why are we analyzing it in this way?

00:00:53.809 --> 00:00:56.579
Because this is an Electoral College election.

00:00:56.579 --> 00:00:58.820
The first candidate to get to 200.

00:00:58.820 --> 00:01:05.770
The only candidate to get to 270 electoral
votes wins overall, new voter registrations.

00:01:05.770 --> 00:01:09.149
And early voting and mail in ballots don't
matter.

00:01:09.149 --> 00:01:14.509
It matters in states that would make a difference
if Democrats have registered way more new

00:01:14.509 --> 00:01:15.929
voters in California.

00:01:15.929 --> 00:01:16.979
Great.

00:01:16.979 --> 00:01:19.020
But Joe Biden's going to win California.

00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:23.430
It's not going to move the needle and get
Joe Biden any more electoral votes.

00:01:23.430 --> 00:01:29.100
Likewise, if we assume that early voting will
be skewed towards Biden.

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:32.090
But Republicans ask for more mail in ballots.

00:01:32.090 --> 00:01:33.609
That would be a red flag.

00:01:33.609 --> 00:01:36.439
And in the states, that could be key.

00:01:36.439 --> 00:01:39.090
There are some numbers that look good for
Trump.

00:01:39.090 --> 00:01:42.200
So let me give you a couple of examples.

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:48.560
Despite Michigan polling having Joe Biden
seven points ahead in terms of mail in ballots

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:55.069
requested in Michigan, Republicans have requested
more mail in ballots than Democrats in Michigan.

00:01:55.069 --> 00:02:00.599
So remember, we were expecting mail in ballots
to be overwhelmingly Biden voters.

00:02:00.599 --> 00:02:03.289
Biden is plus seven in Michigan polling.

00:02:03.289 --> 00:02:09.459
And yet, forty one to thirty nine Republicans
have requested more mail in ballots.

00:02:09.459 --> 00:02:14.599
And in total, if you combine mail in ballot
requests plus early votes, Republicans have

00:02:14.599 --> 00:02:17.230
voted more than Democrats in Michigan.

00:02:17.230 --> 00:02:20.720
That's not a number that I look at and say,
great.

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:22.720
Joe Biden's got Michigan in the bag.

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:27.480
Similarly, if we look at the state of Wisconsin,
which is a very important state, ended up

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:35.190
being extraordinarily important in 2016, despite
Joe Biden leading the polls by six in Wisconsin,

00:02:35.190 --> 00:02:41.180
Republicans in Wisconsin have requested more
mail in ballots by 40 to 38.

00:02:41.180 --> 00:02:46.030
A small margin if you include mail in plus
early voting.

00:02:46.030 --> 00:02:48.769
Republicans are down only 38 to 40.

00:02:48.769 --> 00:02:52.440
And again, Biden supposedly is winning by
six there.

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:58.480
We expect Biden would win the Maylin vote,
but that Trump would win the in-person vote

00:02:58.480 --> 00:02:59.890
on November 3rd.

00:02:59.890 --> 00:03:05.550
What we are seeing so far does not correspond
with the expectations based on polling and

00:03:05.550 --> 00:03:09.939
preferences about voting by mail versus voting
in person.

00:03:09.939 --> 00:03:11.180
These are not good numbers.

00:03:11.180 --> 00:03:13.599
Now, in some other states, things look fine.

00:03:13.599 --> 00:03:17.499
Pennsylvania, for example, which is looking
like it's going to be a key state.

00:03:17.499 --> 00:03:21.230
The numbers in Pennsylvania are very skewed
in favor of Democrats.

00:03:21.230 --> 00:03:23.870
Democrats requesting way more mail in ballots.

00:03:23.870 --> 00:03:29.330
Democrats voting early by a huge majority
in Pennsylvania, like 65 to 25.

00:03:29.330 --> 00:03:31.340
Major margin doesn't mean it's over.

00:03:31.340 --> 00:03:36.579
But the point is, Pennsylvania is looking
much better based on what we expected relative

00:03:36.579 --> 00:03:38.470
to Wisconsin and Michigan.

00:03:38.470 --> 00:03:42.530
The point here is we are, what, 15 days out?

00:03:42.530 --> 00:03:49.290
There is no sense in taking any chances, given
the numbers that we are seeing so far.

00:03:49.290 --> 00:03:53.319
You can find a way to make the numbers look
just great for Joe Biden.

00:03:53.319 --> 00:03:55.450
Just leave it alone.

00:03:55.450 --> 00:04:01.109
Biden is winning today in the popular vote
by more than Hillary was on Election Day 2016.

00:04:01.109 --> 00:04:05.500
But that's not the way that this election
will be decided when you compare.

00:04:05.500 --> 00:04:08.969
Fifteen days out to fifteen days out, the
numbers change.

00:04:08.969 --> 00:04:14.029
When you look at registrations, which I want
to do, the numbers don't look quite so good.

00:04:14.029 --> 00:04:15.859
Let's briefly talk about that.

00:04:15.859 --> 00:04:21.630
Republicans have registered more voters than
Democrats since the primary elections this

00:04:21.630 --> 00:04:27.800
year in the states of Florida, North Carolina
and Pennsylvania.

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:29.020
That's not good.

00:04:29.020 --> 00:04:34.650
It's very difficult to extrapolate that one
number to the results we would get on November

00:04:34.650 --> 00:04:35.690
3rd.

00:04:35.690 --> 00:04:40.699
But it is cause for, if not concern, it is
cause for very much caution.

00:04:40.699 --> 00:04:42.569
I voted on Saturday.

00:04:42.569 --> 00:04:46.560
I published a video of me voting to my Instagram.

00:04:46.560 --> 00:04:49.130
I used a real ballot drop box.

00:04:49.130 --> 00:04:54.210
I think I got about 150 messages from people
saying, David, that doesn't look like a postal

00:04:54.210 --> 00:04:55.849
service mailbox.

00:04:55.849 --> 00:04:57.050
It's because it's not.

00:04:57.050 --> 00:05:05.780
I used an official city of Boston registered,
clearly delineated well-known Dropbox at at

00:05:05.780 --> 00:05:07.400
a state building.

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:08.400
It's a real Dropbox.

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:09.420
I didn't mail my ballot.

00:05:09.420 --> 00:05:10.420
I dropped it off.

00:05:10.420 --> 00:05:11.420
I haven't been tricked.

00:05:11.420 --> 00:05:12.420
It's okay.

00:05:12.420 --> 00:05:13.500
Let's all do it.

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:18.960
Let me know, of course, about any irregularities
that you experience or any trouble whatsoever

00:05:18.960 --> 00:06:41.510
that you run into.

